+
+        # Found live (2026-09-01): imu_pi.py's own equivalent only copies
+        # avg_quat into the published quat while moving() (or on the
+        # just-stopped transition) - fine for real hardware, where a genuine
+        # sensor reading already exists before first motion. For this fake
+        # IMU, imu_sample.quat otherwise stays at its degenerate all-zero
+        # __init__ default forever whenever nothing has ever "moved" yet
+        # (e.g. a stationary Full Simulation session) - _valid_imu_anchor()
+        # then always rejects it (magnitude 0), and every /api/fake_solve
+        # injection silently fails to get a usable IMU anchor no matter how
+        # many times it's retried. A synthetic IMU has no such "hasn't
+        # sampled yet" gap to model - always publish the current avg_quat.
+        imu_sample.moving = imu.moving()
+        imu_sample.quat = quaternion.from_float_array(imu.avg_quat)
